<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masties</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masties was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> ruler in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aures-mountains">Aurès</a> mountains in the late 5th or early 6th century, known only from a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> inscription found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arris">Arris</a>. In it he claims to have been duke for 67 years and emperor for 10, and never to have broken faith with either the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> or the Moors. He is a key witness to the independent Romano-Berber kingdoms that emerged as Vandal rule weakened.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masties.jpg" alt="Masties" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Centre Camille Jullian, C.N.R.S., Aix-en-Provence. · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inscription_de_Masties.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Gaiseric's death the kingdom lost ground to the Berbers: the Kingdom of Altava, <b>Masties</b>'s kingdom of the Aurès in 483–484, Guenfan's Frexenses south of Thugga in 510 and Cabaon's Laguatan, who took Oea and Sabratha and defeated Thrasamund's expedition of 523.</blockquote><a href="/empire/vandal-kingdom">Vandal Kingdom · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>An inscription at Arris records a ruler, <b>Masties</b>, who called himself duke for 67 years and emperor for ten, and claimed never to have broken faith with either Romans or Moors.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-the-aures">Kingdom of the Aures</a></li></ul></section>
